# Shell scripts must keep LF in the working tree, not just in the index.
#
# These run on the VPS under bash, and the pipeline's shell test harness runs
# them locally too. On Windows `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites them to CRLF on
# checkout, and bash then fails on the stray carriage return with errors like
# `$'\r': command not found`. The committed blobs are already LF, so this
# changes nothing about history — it only stops fresh clones and git worktrees
# from producing scripts that cannot run.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Captured upstream payloads, committed verbatim as parser fixtures. `-text`
# turns off both end-of-line conversion and the whitespace linting, because
# neither is a courtesy here: the stockLists capture carries the site's own CRLF
# and tab indentation (its trailing whitespace is part of the cells the marker
# parser has to tolerate), and the futDataDown capture is Big5 bytes, not UTF-8.
# Either file "helpfully" normalised stops being the thing the parser was
# verified against.
# The HTML stays diffable, only its whitespace rules are relaxed; the CSV is
# `binary` because Big5 bytes are not reviewable as a text diff in the first place.
pipeline/tests/fixtures/taifex_stock_lists.html -text whitespace=-trailing-space,-space-before-tab,-tab-in-indent,-indent-with-non-tab
pipeline/tests/fixtures/taifex_fut_history.csv binary
